      "closure_rationale": "Physical structure copying, logical ownership and runtime authority are distinguished. A legal copied-owner function compiles in both C17 compilers; no undefined double-consume is executed. OmmValue self validation rejects ordinary copied controls, while explicitly permitting no claim against malicious public-field edits or retained raw aliases. Opaque representation prevents ordinary field access but does not authenticate identical token holders. Actual ow_move/ow_consume and typed ow_allocator are composed unchanged. The inline owner rebinds self and its internal data pointer, while a heap move preserves the existing typed pointer without allocation. Source poisoning and empty-before-release are explicit. Actual paired GCC/Clang C17 extension diagnostics and C23 recommended-warning/void-cast probes record what compilers enforce without claiming a linear-use type system. Six C17 profiles execute six anchors, six compiled controls and six compiling-stub rejections. Tests cover self and occupied moves, failed allocation, repeated consume, every length1-8, actual OW_MUTANT3/13, slot reuse and cross-registry rejection. The independent630-case generation model varies seven boundary seeds and nine move depths. Cost observations include actual raw registry size and matching release, separate from zero-allocation inline timing. The required changed representation implements self-referential inline relocation and opaque two-slot checked generation authority. Every transfer invalidates old copies; MAX refuses transfer while preserving final consumption and permanent retirement. The harmless local duplicate-holder demonstration proves an identical live copy can act first and invalidate the nominal owner. No crash, arbitrary code execution or authentication guarantee is inferred. Independent delayed learner performance remains unassessed. Bounded author support only."
    },
